      "message": "max\n\nDCP requires the device to ramp current and see where VBUS starts drooping.  Devices are supposed to stop ramping around 1.5A (or maybe 1.8A) even if VBUS is still well within a valid range.  That means depending on the source/device combo, devices may end up pulling anything from 900mA to 2.4A (yes, exceeding the spec)\n\nCDP requires the host to provide 1.5A, guaranteed.",
